  "description": ".NET client library for InferHub — a self-hosted, Ollama-compatible LLM inference mesh. Typed requests over HTTP, dependency-injection friendly, small surface. Point it at a coordinator and call chat, generate (blocking + streaming), embeddings, the vector data-plane (upsert/query/retrieve), opt-in RAG retrieval (grounded chat/generate with source ids), model listing and status from C#. A second interface covers the OpenAI-compatible dialect (/v1/chat/completions, /v1/completions, /v1/embeddings, /v1/models) and the provider steer; a third covers audio — transcription, subtitles, and speech you can stream as it is synthesised. The separate admin client covers fleet ops (list/cordon/drain/uncordon/deregister nodes), vector collection lifecycle (create/drop/rebuild) and the live admin event stream (SSE with reconnect).",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
